   "say": "But he didn't return with nothing. He brought back scholars, architects and books. One of them, an Andalusian poet and architect named Abu Ishaq al-Sahili, is linked to the great Djinguereber Mosque in Timbuktu, built around 1327. It still stands today, almost seven hundred years later.",
