  {
   "chapter": "What it teaches about money",
   "date": "Today",
   "say": "So what can Mansa Musa teach us about money today? Three things. First, wealth that depends on one person rarely outlives him. Second, controlling the trade can matter more than owning the resource. And third, if you flood any market with something, even gold, you make it worth less.",
   "visuals": [
    {
     "type": "title",
     "kicker": "What it teaches",
     "text": "3 Lessons",
     "sub": "about money, from the richest man in history"
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "lines": [
      "1.",
      "Wealth tied to one person",
      "rarely outlives him."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "lines": [
      "2.",
      "Controlling the trade",
      "beats owning the resource."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "lines": [
      "3.",
      "Flood a market,",
      "and you make it worth less."
     ]
    }
   ]
